---
source: crates/motion-format/src/../tests/unit/lib.rs
expression: "report.join(\"\\n\\n\")"
---
## document
`nope` → invalid JSON: expected ident at line 1 column 2; expected a scene object, e.g. {"motion":1,"dur":"5s","layers":[]}
`[]` → invalid type: sequence; expected a scene object, e.g. {"motion":1,"dur":"5s","layers":[]}
`[1,null,null,"1s",null,{},[]]` → invalid type: sequence; expected a scene object, e.g. {"motion":1,"dur":"5s","layers":[]}
`{"motion":1,"layers":[]}` → missing `dur`; expected e.g. "dur":"5s"
`{"dur":"1s","layers":[]}` → missing `motion`; expected e.g. "motion":1
`{"motion":1,"dur":"1s"}` → missing `layers`; expected e.g. "layers":[]
`{"motion":2,"dur":"1s","layers":[]}` → motion: unsupported version 2; expected `1`
`{"motion":"1","dur":"1s","layers":[]}` → motion: invalid type: string "1"; expected a number
`{"motion":1,"dur":null,"layers":[]}` → dur: invalid type: null; expected `<number>f` or `<number>s`, e.g. `12f` or `0.4s`
`{"motion":1,"dur":5,"layers":[]}` → dur: invalid type: integer `5`; expected `<number>f` or `<number>s`, e.g. `12f` or `0.4s`
`{"motion":1,"dur":"soon","layers":[]}` → dur: `soon` is not a valid time; expected `<number>f` or `<number>s`, e.g. `12f` or `0.4s`
`{"motion":1,"dur":"1s","fps":null,"layers":[]}` → fps: invalid type: null; expected a number
`{"motion":1,"dur":"1s","fps":"a, expected b","layers":[]}` → fps: invalid type: string "a, expected b"; expected a number
`{"motion":1,"dur":"1s","fps":0,"layers":[]}` → fps: must be a number above zero; expected e.g. `30`
`{"motion":1,"dur":"1s","size":null,"layers":[]}` → size: invalid type: null; expected a size name such as `1080p`, or `<width>x<height>`
`{"motion":1,"dur":"1s","size":3,"layers":[]}` → size: invalid type: integer `3`; expected a size name such as `1080p`, or `<width>x<height>`
`{"motion":1,"dur":"1s","size":"huge","layers":[]}` → size: unknown size `huge`; expected one of 720p, 1080p, 4k, square, vertical, or <width>x<height>
`{"motion":1,"dur":"1s","bg":0,"layers":[]}` → bg: invalid type: integer `0`; expected `#RGB`, `#RRGGBB` or `#RRGGBBAA`
`{"motion":1,"dur":"1s","colour":"x","layers":[]}` → colour: unknown field `colour`; expected one of motion, size, fps, dur, bg, shutter, labels, presets, fonts, slots, roles, locks, comps, layers
`{"motion":1,"dur":"1s","layers":{}}` → layers: invalid type: map; expected a list of layer objects, e.g. [{"id":"box","rect":"100x100"}]

## layers
`1` → layers[0]: invalid type: integer `1`; expected a layer object, e.g. {"id":"box","rect":"100x100"}
`["a","hi"]` → layers[0]: invalid type: sequence; expected a layer object, e.g. {"id":"box","rect":"100x100"}
`{"rect":"1x1"}` → layers[0]: missing `id`; expected e.g. "id":"title"
`{"id":3,"rect":"1x1"}` → layers[0].id: invalid type: integer `3`; expected a string
`{"id":1.5,"rect":"1x1"}` → layers[0].id: invalid type: floating point `1.5`; expected a string
`{"id":1e300,"rect":"1x1"}` → layers[0].id: invalid type: floating point `1e300`; expected a string
`{"id":"Bad Id","rect":"1x1"}` → layers[0].id: invalid id `Bad Id`; expected ids use lowercase letters, digits, `-` and `_`, starting with a letter
`{"id":"scene","rect":"1x1"}` → layers[0].id: `scene` names the scene itself, so no layer may take it; expected another id, such as `scene-2`
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1"},{"id":"a","rect":"1x1"}` → layers[1].id: duplicate id `a`; expected every layer to have its own id
`{"id":"a"}` → a: needs exactly one of `text`, `rect`, `shapes`, `comp`, `image`, `video`, `audio` or `pivot`, or only `fx` for a filter layer; expected e.g. "text":"Hello", "rect":"300x100", "shapes":[…], "comp":"card", "image":"photo.jpg", "video":"clip.mov", "audio":"music.mp3" or "pivot":true
`{"id":"a","fx":[]}` → a: needs exactly one of `text`, `rect`, `shapes`, `comp`, `image`, `video`, `audio` or `pivot`, or only `fx` for a filter layer; expected e.g. "text":"Hello", "rect":"300x100", "shapes":[…], "comp":"card", "image":"photo.jpg", "video":"clip.mov", "audio":"music.mp3" or "pivot":true
`{"id":"a","fx":[{"fill":"#FFFFFF"}],"fill":"#000000"}` → a.fill: `fill` only applies to `text` or `rect` layers; expected `fill` only next to `text` or `rect`
`{"id":"a","fx":[{"fill":"#FFFFFF"}],"box":[1,1]}` → a.box: `box` only applies to `text` or `image` or `video` layers; expected `box` only next to `text` or `image` or `video`
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","adjust":true}` → a.adjust: `adjust` applies the layer's `fx` to what is below it, and it has none; expected "fx":[{"fill":"#FFFFFF"}] next to "adjust":true
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","adjust":1,"fx":[]}` → a.adjust: invalid type: integer `1`; expected a boolean
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","collapse":true}` → a.collapse: `collapse` only applies to `comp` layers; expected `collapse` only next to `comp`
`{"id":"a","audio":""}` → a.audio: an empty audio path; expected a WAV, MP3, FLAC or Ogg Vorbis file, relative to the scene file, e.g. `music/theme.mp3`
`{"id":"a","audio":"x.mp3","box":[1,1]}` → a.box: `box` only applies to `text` or `image` or `video` layers; expected `box` only next to `text` or `image` or `video`
`{"id":"a","audio":"x.mp3","fx":[{"fill":"#FFFFFF"}]}` → a.fx: an audio layer draws nothing, so it has nothing for effects to change; expected `fx` on a layer that draws
`{"id":"s","audio":"x.mp3"},{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","matte":"s"}` → a.matte: `s` is an audio layer, which draws nothing to matte with; expected a layer that draws
`{"id":"m","rect":"1x1"},{"id":"a","audio":"x.mp3","matte":"m"}` → a.matte: an audio layer draws nothing, so it has nothing for a matte to cut; expected `matte` on a layer that draws
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","volume":0.5}` → a.volume: `volume` only applies to `audio` or `comp` layers, which play sound; expected `volume` on an audio layer, or on a `comp` layer for its whole sound
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","anim":{"volume":"0 -> 1 @0-5f"}}` → a.volume: `volume` only applies to `audio` or `comp` layers, which play sound; expected `volume` on an audio layer, or on a `comp` layer for its whole sound
`{"id":"a","audio":"x.mp3","volume":5}` → a.volume: value 5 is outside 0..=4; expected a number from 0 to 4
`{"id":"a","fx":[{"fill":"#FFFFFF"}],"collapse":true}` → a.collapse: `collapse` only applies to `comp` layers; expected `collapse` only next to `comp`
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","text":"x"}` → a.rect: needs exactly one of `text`, `rect`, `shapes`, `comp`, `image`, `video`, `audio` or `pivot`, or only `fx` for a filter layer; expected e.g. "text":"Hello", "rect":"300x100", "shapes":[…], "comp":"card", "image":"photo.jpg", "video":"clip.mov", "audio":"music.mp3" or "pivot":true
`{"id":"a","text":null}` → a.text: invalid type: null; expected a string
`{"id":"a","text":3}` → a.text: invalid type: integer `3`; expected a string
`{"id":"a","rect":1}` → a.rect: invalid type: integer `1`; expected `<width>x<height> [r<radius>]`, e.g. `300x400 r24`
`{"id":"a","text":"x","font":1}` → a.font: invalid type: integer `1`; expected `<family> <size> [<weight>]`, e.g. `Inter 96 700`
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","font":"Inter 9"}` → a.font: `font` only applies to `text` layers; expected `font` only next to `text`
`{"id":"a","image":"a.png"}` → a: missing `box`: an image layer fills its box; expected the picture's size in px, e.g. "box":[1920,1080]
`{"id":"a","image":"","box":[1,1]}` → a.image: an empty image path; expected a PNG or JPEG file, relative to the scene file, e.g. `photos/beach.jpg`
`{"id":"a","image":"a.png","box":[0,1]}` → a.box: a box's width and height are above zero; expected `[width, height]` from the layer's origin, or `[x, y, width, height]` from the box's top-left corner, in px, the sizes above zero, e.g. `[600, 300]` or `[-300, -150, 600, 300]`
`{"id":"a","image":3,"box":[1,1]}` → a.image: invalid type: integer `3`; expected a string
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","fill":1}` → a.fill: 1 numbers do not make a colour; expected a colour: `#RGB`, `#RRGGBB`, `#RRGGBBAA`, or `[r, g, b, a]` with each channel 0 to 1
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","fill":"red"}` → a.fill: `red` is not a colour; expected a colour: `#RGB`, `#RRGGBB`, `#RRGGBBAA`, or `[r, g, b, a]` with each channel 0 to 1
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","at":1}` → a.at: invalid type: integer `1`; expected `<x> <y>`, each a number of pixels or `center`, e.g. `center 260`
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","in":null}` → a.in: invalid type: null; expected `<preset> [<n>px] [<n>f|<n>s] [<curve>] [@<time>] [char|char-no-space|word|line] [stagger <time>] [first|last|center|edges|random]`, e.g. `fade-up 40px 12f ease-out @0f` or `fade-up word stagger 3f`; a curve is a name such as `ease-out`, `out-expo` or `hold`, `out-back(2)`, `steps(4)`, `spring(.3)`, or `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)`
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","in":true}` → a.in: invalid type: boolean `true`; expected `<preset> [<n>px] [<n>f|<n>s] [<curve>] [@<time>] [char|char-no-space|word|line] [stagger <time>] [first|last|center|edges|random]`, e.g. `fade-up 40px 12f ease-out @0f` or `fade-up word stagger 3f`; a curve is a name such as `ease-out`, `out-expo` or `hold`, `out-back(2)`, `steps(4)`, `spring(.3)`, or `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)`
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","in":"zoom"}` → a.in: unknown preset `zoom`; expected one of fade, fade-up, fade-down, fade-left, fade-right, pop, spin-in
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","anim":null}` → a.anim: invalid type: null; expected an object of property tracks, e.g. {"opacity":"0 -> 1 @0-12f"}
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","anim":[]}` → a.anim: invalid type: sequence; expected an object of property tracks, e.g. {"opacity":"0 -> 1 @0-12f"}
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","x":1}` → a.x: unknown layer key `x`; expected one of id, text, rect, shapes, comp, overrides, image, video, audio, pivot, font, fill, style, runs, paragraphs, box, animate, at, in, anim, parent, span, offset, stretch, mask, fx, adjust, collapse, hidden, matte, blend, mblur, position, anchor, scale, rotate, opacity, volume
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","at":"1 2","position":[1,2]}` → a.position: `position` and `at` both place the layer; expected one of them: "at":"540 960" places it in the parent's box, "position":[540,960] at an exact point in the parent's own coordinates
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","rotate":"x"}` → a.rotate: `x` is not a number; expected a number, e.g. `0.5`
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","scale":[1,2,3]}` → a.scale: 3 numbers do not make a point; expected a point, `[x, y]` in JSON or `x,y` in a string, e.g. `[540, 960]`
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","opacity":2}` → a.opacity: value 2 is outside 0..=1; expected a number from 0 to 1
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","parent":"b"}` → a.parent: unknown layer id `b`; expected one of a
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","parent":"a"}` → a.parent: `a` would move with itself through its parents; expected parents that never lead back to the layer
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","parent":"b"},{"id":"b","rect":"1x1","parent":"a"}` → a.parent: `a` would move with itself through its parents; expected parents that never lead back to the layer
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","parent":3}` → a.parent: invalid type: integer `3`; expected a string
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","matte":"b"}` → a.matte: unknown layer id `b`; expected one of a
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","matte":"a"}` → a.matte: `a` would be its own matte through its mattes; expected mattes that never lead back to the layer
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","matte":"b"},{"id":"b","rect":"1x1","matte":"a luma"}` → a.matte: `a` would be its own matte through its mattes; expected mattes that never lead back to the layer
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","matte":"b sideways"},{"id":"b","rect":"1x1"}` → a.matte: unknown matte mode `sideways`; expected one of alpha, alpha-inverted, luma, luma-inverted
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","matte":"b alpha extra"},{"id":"b","rect":"1x1"}` → a.matte: `b alpha extra` is not a valid matte; expected `<layer id> [alpha|alpha-inverted|luma|luma-inverted]`, e.g. `reveal alpha`
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","matte":true}` → a.matte: invalid type: boolean `true`; expected `<layer id> [alpha|alpha-inverted|luma|luma-inverted]`, e.g. `reveal alpha`
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","fx":[{"displacement-map":5,"map":"b"}]}` → a.fx[0].map: unknown layer id `b`; expected one of a
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","fx":[{"displacement-map":5,"map":"a"}]}` → a: `a` would read its own drawing through the layers its effects read; expected effects that read other layers, never leading back
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","fx":[{"displacement-map":5,"map":"b"}]},{"id":"b","rect":"1x1","matte":"a"}` → a: `a` would read its own drawing through the layers its effects read; expected effects that read other layers, never leading back
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","fx":[{"displacement-map":5,"map":3}]}` → a.fx[0].map: invalid type: integer `3`; expected a string
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","fx":[{"audio-spectrum":5,"audio":"b"}]},{"id":"b","rect":"1x1"}` → a.fx[0].audio: `b` plays no sound; expected an `audio` layer, or a `comp` layer for its composition's sound
`{"id":"m","audio":"m.wav"},{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","fx":[{"displacement-map":5,"map":"m"}]}` → a.fx[0].map: `m` is an audio layer, which draws nothing to read; expected a layer that draws
`{"id":"m","audio":"m.wav"},{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","fx":[{"audio-waveform":5,"audio":"m","channel":"middle"}]}` → a.fx[0].channel: unknown audio-waveform channel `middle`; expected one of mono, left, right
`{"id":"m","audio":"m.wav"},{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","anim":{"scale":"1 -> 2 -> 3 @level m"}}` → a.anim.scale: a track that listens goes from one value at silence to one at full level, not `1 -> 2 -> 3`; expected "<value> -> <value> @level <layer> [<low>-<high>Hz] [smooth <time>] [<curve>]", e.g. "1 -> 1.25 @level music 30-150Hz smooth 0.06s out-quad"
`{"id":"m","audio":"m.wav"},{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","anim":{"scale":"1 -> 2 @level"}}` → a.anim.scale: missing the layer `@level` listens to; expected "<value> -> <value> @level <layer> [<low>-<high>Hz] [smooth <time>] [<curve>]", e.g. "1 -> 1.25 @level music 30-150Hz smooth 0.06s out-quad"
`{"id":"m","audio":"m.wav"},{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","anim":{"scale":"1 -> 2 @level m 5-2Hz"}}` → a.anim.scale: `5-2Hz` is not a band of frequencies; expected `<low>-<high>Hz` with 0 < low < high, e.g. `30-150Hz`
`{"id":"m","audio":"m.wav"},{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","anim":{"scale":"1 -> 2 @level m smooth"}}` → a.anim.scale: missing the time after `smooth`; expected "<value> -> <value> @level <layer> [<low>-<high>Hz] [smooth <time>] [<curve>]", e.g. "1 -> 1.25 @level music 30-150Hz smooth 0.06s out-quad"
`{"id":"m","audio":"m.wav"},{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","anim":{"scale":"1 -> 2 @level m linear extra"}}` → a.anim.scale: unexpected `extra` after the curve; expected "<value> -> <value> @level <layer> [<low>-<high>Hz] [smooth <time>] [<curve>]", e.g. "1 -> 1.25 @level music 30-150Hz smooth 0.06s out-quad"
`{"id":"b","rect":"1x1"},{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","anim":{"scale":"1 -> 2 @level b"}}` → a.anim.scale: `b` plays no sound to follow; expected an `audio` layer, or a `comp` layer for its composition's sound
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","anim":{"scale":"1 -> 2 @level zz"}}` → a.anim.scale: unknown layer id `zz`; expected one of a
`{"id":"m","audio":"m.wav","anim":{"volume":"0 -> 1 @level m"}}` → m.anim.volume: `volume` cannot follow a sound's level, which it would change; expected a property other than `volume`
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","fx":[{"fill":"#FF0000","anim":{"opacity":"0 -> 1 @level q"}}]}` → a.fx[0].anim.opacity: unknown layer id `q`; expected one of a
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","fx":[{"fill":"#FF0000","map":"a"}]}` → a.fx[0].map: unknown fill key `map`; expected one of fill, id, hidden, anim, opacity
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","span":"5f"}` → a.span: `5f` has no `-` between start and end; expected `<start>-<end>` with a unit, e.g. `0-30f`, `0.5s-1s`; a bare start takes the end's unit
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","span":"5-1f"}` → a.span: `5f-1f` starts after it ends; expected `<start>-<end>` with a unit, e.g. `0-30f`, `0.5s-1s`; a bare start takes the end's unit
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","offset":"-1x"}` → a.offset: `-1x` is not a time or a moment; expected a time such as `2s` or `-6f`, or a base moved by a time: a label (`cta`, `cta+12f`, `cta-0.5s`), `<` where the layer before ends (`<+6f`) or `<<` where it starts (`<<-3f`)
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","stretch":0}` → a.stretch: must be a number other than zero; expected e.g. `2` for half speed, `-1` for backwards
`{"id":"a","rect":"10x10","in":"fade-up","anim":{"opacity":"0 -> 1 @0-5f"}}` → a.anim.opacity: `opacity` is already animated by `in` (preset `fade-up`); expected `a in=none anim={"opacity":"0 -> 1 @0-12f ease-out","y":"580 -> 540 @0-12f ease-out"}` (the entrance as anim tracks; then adjust `opacity`), or define a scene preset without `opacity` under "presets"
`{"id":"a","rect":"10x10","in":"fade-up","anim":{"position":"0,0 -> 1,1 @0-5f"}}` → a.anim.position: `position` is already animated by `in` (preset `fade-up`); expected `a in=none anim={"opacity":"0 -> 1 @0-12f ease-out","y":"580 -> 540 @0-12f ease-out","position":"0,0 -> 1,1 @0-5f"}` (the entrance as anim tracks; then adjust `position`), or define a scene preset without `position` under "presets"

## overrides
`"overrides":3` → card.overrides: invalid type: integer `3`; expected an object of layer keys by layer address and slot values by `$id`, e.g. {"title":{"text":"Sale"},"$accent":"#E63946"}
`"overrides":{"title":3}` → card.overrides.title: `3` is not an object of layer keys; expected an object of layer keys, e.g. {"text":"Sale"}
`"overrides":{"ghost":{"text":"x"}}` → card.overrides: unknown layer `ghost`; expected one of title
`"overrides":{"title.text":{}}` → card.overrides: `title.text` is not the address of a layer; expected a layer of the composition, e.g. `title` or `badge/icon`, or a slot, `$accent`
`"overrides":{"title":{"id":"other"}}` → card.overrides: an override of `title` sets its `id`; expected the keys to change; the id stays the layer's own
`"overrides":{"title":{"text":5}}` → card/title.text: invalid type: integer `5`; expected a string
`"overrides":{"title":{"rect":"1x1"}}` → card/title.rect: needs exactly one of `text`, `rect`, `shapes`, `comp`, `image`, `video`, `audio` or `pivot`, or only `fx` for a filter layer; expected e.g. "text":"Hello", "rect":"300x100", "shapes":[…], "comp":"card", "image":"photo.jpg", "video":"clip.mov", "audio":"music.mp3" or "pivot":true
`"overrides":{"title":{"fill":"red"}}` → card/title.fill: `red` is not a colour; expected a colour: `#RGB`, `#RRGGBB`, `#RRGGBBAA`, or `[r, g, b, a]` with each channel 0 to 1
`"overrides":{"title/x":{"text":"x"}}` → card/title.overrides: `overrides` only applies to `comp` layers; expected `overrides` only next to `comp`
`"overrides":{"title":{"zoom":1}}` → card/title.zoom: unknown layer key `zoom`; expected one of id, text, rect, shapes, comp, overrides, image, video, audio, pivot, font, fill, style, runs, paragraphs, box, animate, at, in, anim, parent, span, offset, stretch, mask, fx, adjust, collapse, hidden, matte, blend, mblur, position, anchor, scale, rotate, opacity, volume
`"overrides":{"$ghost":"x"}` → card.overrides.$ghost: unknown slot `$ghost`; expected a slot of the composition, which declares none

## collapse
`"collapse":1` → card.collapse: invalid type: integer `1`; expected a boolean
`"collapse":true,"adjust":true,"fx":[{"fill":"#FFFFFF"}]` → card.collapse: `adjust` keeps the layer from drawing, so it has nothing to `collapse`; expected `adjust` or `collapse`, not both

## overrides on a layer that draws no composition
`"overrides":{"x":{}}` → a.overrides: `overrides` only applies to `comp` layers; expected `overrides` only next to `comp`

## anim
`"x":3` → a.anim.x: invalid type: integer `3`; expected "<value> -> <value>[@<n>%] ... -> <value> @<start>-<end> [<curve>]", e.g. "0 -> 1 @0-12f ease-out" or "rest+40 -> rest @0-12f", or a list of keys, each [time, value, curve] or {"t":time,"v":value,"curve":curve,"path":[[out-x,out-y],[in-x,in-y]]}
`"glow":"0 -> 1 @0-5f"` → a.anim.glow: unknown layer property `glow`; expected one of position, anchor, scale, rotate, opacity, volume, x, y, anchor-x, anchor-y, scale-x, scale-y
`"x":"0 1 @0-5f"` → a.anim.x: missing `->` after the start value in `0 1 @0-5f`; expected "<value> -> <value>[@<n>%] ... -> <value> @<start>-<end> [<curve>]", e.g. "0 -> 1 @0-12f ease-out", "0 -> 200@40% -> 150 @0-30f" or "rest+40 -> rest @0-12f"
`"x":"0 -> 1 @5-0f"` → a.anim.x: `@5f-0f` starts after it ends; expected `@<start>-<end>` with a unit, e.g. `@0-30f`, `@0.5s-1s`
`"x":"inf -> 1 @0-5f"` → a.anim.x: `inf` is not a number; expected a number, e.g. `0.5`
`"x":"a -> 1 @0-5f"` → a.anim.x: `a` is not a number; expected a number, e.g. `0.5`
`"x":"rest*x -> rest @0-5f"` → a.anim.x: `rest*x` is not a value against the rest; expected `rest`, `rest+<value>`, `rest-<value>` or `rest*<factor>`, e.g. `rest+40`, `rest+0,-40` or `rest*1.2`, on a number or a point
`"x":[[0,"rest/2"],[5,"rest"]]` → a.anim.x[0][1]: `rest/2` is not a value against the rest; expected `rest`, `rest+<value>`, `rest-<value>` or `rest*<factor>`, e.g. `rest+40`, `rest+0,-40` or `rest*1.2`, on a number or a point
`"scale":"1,2,3 -> 1 @0-5f"` → a.anim.scale: `1,2,3` is not a point; expected a point, `[x, y]` in JSON or `x,y` in a string, e.g. `[540, 960]`
`"position":"1 -> 2 @0-5f"` → a.anim.position: `1` is not a point; expected a point, `[x, y]` in JSON or `x,y` in a string, e.g. `[540, 960]`
`"fill":"0 -> 1 @0-5f"` → a.anim.fill: unknown layer property `fill`; expected one of position, anchor, scale, rotate, opacity, volume, x, y, anchor-x, anchor-y, scale-x, scale-y
`"x":"0 -> 1 @0-5f","position":"0,0 -> 1,1 @0-5f"` → a.anim.position: `x` and `position` both animate `position`; expected `position` animated whole, or its components `x`, `y` one at a time
`"position":[[0,[1,2],["linear","linear"]]]` → a.anim.position[0][2]: `position` moves along a path, so one curve times the whole move; expected one curve, or animate x and y one at a time
`"scale":[[0,[1,2],["linear"]]]` → a.anim.scale[0][2]: 1 curves for 2 components; expected a curve such as "ease-out", or a list of curves, one per component, e.g. ["ease-out","linear"]
`"scale":[[0,[1,2],["linear","bouncy"]]]` → a.anim.scale[0][2][1]: unknown curve `bouncy`; expected one of linear, hold, ease, ease-in, ease-out, ease-in-out, or <shape>-<family> (e.g. out-expo) or cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2) or speed(out,out-reach,in,in-reach) or steps(n) or spring(bounce)
`"scale":[[0,[1,2],3]]` → a.anim.scale[0][2]: invalid type: integer `3`; expected a curve such as "ease-out", or a list of curves, one per component, e.g. ["ease-out","linear"]
`"x":[{"t":0,"v":1,"path":[[0,0],[0,0]]}]` → a.anim.x[0].path: `x` does not move along a path; expected [[out-x, out-y], [in-x, in-y]]: the bend leaving this key, as an offset from its value, and the bend arriving at the next key, as an offset from that key's value
`"position":[{"t":0,"v":[1,2],"path":[[0,0]]}]` → a.anim.position[0].path: invalid length 1; expected an array of length 2
`"position":[{"t":0,"v":[1,2],"bend":1}]` → a.anim.position[0].bend: unknown field `bend`; expected one of t, v, curve, path
`"position":[{"v":[1,2]}]` → a.anim.position[0]: missing field `t`
`"x":[[0,1,"speed(0,2,0,0)"]]` → a.anim.x[0][2]: `speed(0,2,0,0)`: each reach must be between 0 and 1; expected `speed(out,out-reach,in,in-reach)` (no spaces): the speed leaving the key and arriving at the next, in value units per second, each with how far into the span it reaches, 0 to 1, e.g. `speed(0,.33,0,.33)`
`"opacity":"0 -> 2 @0-5f"` → a.anim.opacity: value 2 is outside 0..=1; expected a number from 0 to 1
`"x":[]` → a.anim.x: needs at least one key; expected a list of keys like [[0, 0], ["12f", 1, "ease-out"]]
`"x":[5]` → a.anim.x[0]: invalid type: integer `5`; expected [time, value] or [time, value, curve], e.g. ["12f", 1, "ease-out"], or {"t":time,"v":value,"curve":curve,"path":[[out-x,out-y],[in-x,in-y]]}
`"x":[[0]]` → a.anim.x[0]: invalid length 1; expected [time, value] or [time, value, curve], e.g. ["12f", 1, "ease-out"], or {"t":time,"v":value,"curve":curve,"path":[[out-x,out-y],[in-x,in-y]]}
`"x":[[0, 1, "linear", 4]]` → a.anim.x[0]: invalid length 4; expected [time, value] or [time, value, curve], e.g. ["12f", 1, "ease-out"], or {"t":time,"v":value,"curve":curve,"path":[[out-x,out-y],[in-x,in-y]]}
`"x":[[true, 0]]` → a.anim.x[0][0]: invalid type: boolean `true`; expected a frame count, or a time such as `12f` or `-0.4s`
`"x":[["12", 0]]` → a.anim.x[0]: `12` is not a valid time; expected `<number>f` or `<number>s`, which may be negative, e.g. `12f` or `-0.4s`
`"x":[["-1x", 0]]` → a.anim.x[0]: `-1x` is not a valid time; expected `<number>f` or `<number>s`, which may be negative, e.g. `12f` or `-0.4s`
`"x":[[0, "a"]]` → a.anim.x[0][1]: `a` is not a number; expected a number, e.g. `0.5`
`"x":[[0, 1, 3]]` → a.anim.x[0][2]: invalid type: integer `3`; expected a curve such as "ease-out", or a list of curves, one per component, e.g. ["ease-out","linear"]
`"x":[[0, 1, null]]` → a.anim.x[0][2]: invalid type: null; expected a curve such as "ease-out", or a list of curves, one per component, e.g. ["ease-out","linear"]
`"x":[[0, 1, "nope"]]` → a.anim.x[0][2]: unknown curve `nope`; expected one of linear, hold, ease, ease-in, ease-out, ease-in-out, or <shape>-<family> (e.g. out-expo) or cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2) or speed(out,out-reach,in,in-reach) or steps(n) or spring(bounce)
`"x":[[5, 0], [2, 1]]` → a.anim.x[1]: key is earlier than the one before it; expected keys in time order, earliest first
`"opacity":[[0, 0], [5, 1], [9, 2]]` → a.anim.opacity[2][1]: value 2 is outside 0..=1; expected a number from 0 to 1

## presets
`null` → presets: invalid type: null; expected an object of presets, e.g. {"slide":{"opacity":0,"x":"-d"}}
`[]` → presets: invalid type: sequence; expected an object of presets, e.g. {"slide":{"opacity":0,"x":"-d"}}
`{"a":3}` → presets.a: invalid type: integer `3`; expected an object of property starts, e.g. {"opacity":0,"y":"+d"}
`{"Bad":{"x":1}}` → presets.Bad: invalid preset name `Bad`; expected ids use lowercase letters, digits, `-` and `_`, starting with a letter
`{"x":{}}` → presets.x: preset `x` sets no properties; expected e.g. {"opacity":0}
`{"a":{"zoom":1}}` → presets.a.zoom: unknown layer property `zoom`; expected one of position, anchor, scale, rotate, opacity, volume, x, y, anchor-x, anchor-y, scale-x, scale-y
`{"a":{"x":true}}` → presets.a.x: invalid type: boolean `true`; expected a number, "+d" or "-d"
`{"a":{"x":"left"}}` → presets.a.x: invalid value: string "left"; expected a number, "+d" or "-d"
`{"a":{"x":"l, expected q"}}` → presets.a.x: invalid value: string "l, expected q"; expected a number, "+d" or "-d"
`{"a":{"opacity":2}}` → presets.a.opacity: value 2 is outside 0..=1; expected a number from 0 to 1
`{"dim":{"opacity":"-d"}}` → presets.dim.opacity: `opacity` is not a number of pixels, so it cannot start at a distance; expected a value of its own, e.g. 0

## unknown preset with scene presets
`{"slide":{"x":1},"fade":{"y":1}}` → a.in: unknown preset `zoom`; expected one of slide, fade, fade-up, fade-down, fade-left, fade-right, pop, spin-in

## time
`12` → `12` is not a valid time; expected `<number>f` or `<number>s`, e.g. `12f` or `0.4s`

## colour
`red` → `red` is not a valid colour; expected `#RGB`, `#RRGGBB` or `#RRGGBBAA`

## size
`8k` → unknown size `8k`; expected one of 720p, 1080p, 4k, square, vertical, or <width>x<height>
`640x` → `640x` is not a valid size; expected `<width>x<height>`, each a whole number of pixels above zero, e.g. `1920x1080`
`640x360 ` → unexpected text after the size `640x360` in `640x360 `; expected `<width>x<height>`, each a whole number of pixels above zero, e.g. `1920x1080`
`1x2x3` → unexpected text after the size `1x2` in `1x2x3`; expected `<width>x<height>`, each a whole number of pixels above zero, e.g. `1920x1080`

## curve
`foo` → unknown curve `foo`; expected one of linear, hold, ease, ease-in, ease-out, ease-in-out, or <shape>-<family> (e.g. out-expo) or cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2) or speed(out,out-reach,in,in-reach) or steps(n) or spring(bounce)
`cubic(.2,0,0,1` → `cubic(.2,0,0,1` is missing its closing `)`; expected `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)` (no spaces) with x1 and x2 between 0 and 1, e.g. `cubic(.2,0,0,1)`
`cubic(0,0,1,1)x` → `cubic(0,0,1,1)x` is missing its closing `)`; expected `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)` (no spaces) with x1 and x2 between 0 and 1, e.g. `cubic(.2,0,0,1)`
`cubic(.2,0,1)` → `cubic(.2,0,1)` needs four numbers; expected `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)` (no spaces) with x1 and x2 between 0 and 1, e.g. `cubic(.2,0,0,1)`
`cubic(1,2))` → `cubic(1,2))` needs four numbers; expected `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)` (no spaces) with x1 and x2 between 0 and 1, e.g. `cubic(.2,0,0,1)`
`cubic(1.2,0,0,1)` → `cubic(1.2,0,0,1)`: x1 and x2 must be between 0 and 1; expected `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)` (no spaces) with x1 and x2 between 0 and 1, e.g. `cubic(.2,0,0,1)`

## rect
`300` → `300` is not a valid rectangle; expected `<width>x<height> [r<radius>]`, e.g. `300x400 r24`

## position
`260` → `260` is not a valid position; expected `<x> <y>`, each a number of pixels or `center`, e.g. `center 260`

## font
`Inter` → `Inter` has no size; expected `<family> <size> [<weight>]`, e.g. `Inter 96 700`
`96 700` → `96 700` has no font family; expected `<family> <size> [<weight>]`, e.g. `Inter 96 700`
`1 2 3` → `1 2 3` has no font family; expected `<family> <size> [<weight>]`, e.g. `Inter 96 700`
`Inter 0` → `0` is not a valid size; it must be above zero; expected `<family> <size> [<weight>]`, e.g. `Inter 96 700`
`Inter 96 700 750` → `750` is not a valid weight; the weight must be 100, 200 … 900; expected `<family> <size> [<weight>]`, e.g. `Inter 96 700`
`Baloo 2 120` → `Baloo 2 120` is ambiguous: if the family name ends in a number, write the size and weight explicitly, e.g. `Baloo 2 120 400`; otherwise the weight must be 100, 200 … 900; expected `<family> <size> [<weight>]`, e.g. `Inter 96 700`

## behaviour
`` → a behaviour needs a preset; expected `<preset> [<n>px] [<n>f|<n>s] [<curve>] [@<time>] [char|char-no-space|word|line] [stagger <time>] [first|last|center|edges|random]`, e.g. `fade-up 40px 12f ease-out @0f` or `fade-up word stagger 3f`; a curve is a name such as `ease-out`, `out-expo` or `hold`, `out-back(2)`, `steps(4)`, `spring(.3)`, or `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)`
`Fade-Up` → `Fade-Up` is not a valid preset name; ids use lowercase letters, digits, `-` and `_`, starting with a letter; expected `<preset> [<n>px] [<n>f|<n>s] [<curve>] [@<time>] [char|char-no-space|word|line] [stagger <time>] [first|last|center|edges|random]`, e.g. `fade-up 40px 12f ease-out @0f` or `fade-up word stagger 3f`; a curve is a name such as `ease-out`, `out-expo` or `hold`, `out-back(2)`, `steps(4)`, `spring(.3)`, or `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)`
`fade 12x` → unknown token `12x`; expected `<preset> [<n>px] [<n>f|<n>s] [<curve>] [@<time>] [char|char-no-space|word|line] [stagger <time>] [first|last|center|edges|random]`, e.g. `fade-up 40px 12f ease-out @0f` or `fade-up word stagger 3f`; a curve is a name such as `ease-out`, `out-expo` or `hold`, `out-back(2)`, `steps(4)`, `spring(.3)`, or `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)`
`fade -3f` → `-3f` is not a valid duration; expected `<preset> [<n>px] [<n>f|<n>s] [<curve>] [@<time>] [char|char-no-space|word|line] [stagger <time>] [first|last|center|edges|random]`, e.g. `fade-up 40px 12f ease-out @0f` or `fade-up word stagger 3f`; a curve is a name such as `ease-out`, `out-expo` or `hold`, `out-back(2)`, `steps(4)`, `spring(.3)`, or `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)`
`fade 1pxpx` → `1pxpx` is not a valid distance; expected `<preset> [<n>px] [<n>f|<n>s] [<curve>] [@<time>] [char|char-no-space|word|line] [stagger <time>] [first|last|center|edges|random]`, e.g. `fade-up 40px 12f ease-out @0f` or `fade-up word stagger 3f`; a curve is a name such as `ease-out`, `out-expo` or `hold`, `out-back(2)`, `steps(4)`, `spring(.3)`, or `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)`
`fade @12` → `@12` is not a valid start time; expected `<preset> [<n>px] [<n>f|<n>s] [<curve>] [@<time>] [char|char-no-space|word|line] [stagger <time>] [first|last|center|edges|random]`, e.g. `fade-up 40px 12f ease-out @0f` or `fade-up word stagger 3f`; a curve is a name such as `ease-out`, `out-expo` or `hold`, `out-back(2)`, `steps(4)`, `spring(.3)`, or `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)`
`fade stagger 3f` → `stagger 3f` orders the parts of a text, so it needs them: add `char`, `char-no-space`, `word` or `line`; expected `<preset> [<n>px] [<n>f|<n>s] [<curve>] [@<time>] [char|char-no-space|word|line] [stagger <time>] [first|last|center|edges|random]`, e.g. `fade-up 40px 12f ease-out @0f` or `fade-up word stagger 3f`; a curve is a name such as `ease-out`, `out-expo` or `hold`, `out-back(2)`, `steps(4)`, `spring(.3)`, or `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)`
`fade word stagger` → `stagger` needs the time each part waits, such as `stagger 3f`; expected `<preset> [<n>px] [<n>f|<n>s] [<curve>] [@<time>] [char|char-no-space|word|line] [stagger <time>] [first|last|center|edges|random]`, e.g. `fade-up 40px 12f ease-out @0f` or `fade-up word stagger 3f`; a curve is a name such as `ease-out`, `out-expo` or `hold`, `out-back(2)`, `steps(4)`, `spring(.3)`, or `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)`
`fade word stagger soon center` → `soon` is not a valid stagger time; expected `<preset> [<n>px] [<n>f|<n>s] [<curve>] [@<time>] [char|char-no-space|word|line] [stagger <time>] [first|last|center|edges|random]`, e.g. `fade-up 40px 12f ease-out @0f` or `fade-up word stagger 3f`; a curve is a name such as `ease-out`, `out-expo` or `hold`, `out-back(2)`, `steps(4)`, `spring(.3)`, or `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)`
`fade word line` → parts given twice: `word` and `line`; expected `<preset> [<n>px] [<n>f|<n>s] [<curve>] [@<time>] [char|char-no-space|word|line] [stagger <time>] [first|last|center|edges|random]`, e.g. `fade-up 40px 12f ease-out @0f` or `fade-up word stagger 3f`; a curve is a name such as `ease-out`, `out-expo` or `hold`, `out-back(2)`, `steps(4)`, `spring(.3)`, or `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)`
`fade bounce` → unknown curve `bounce`; expected one of linear, hold, ease, ease-in, ease-out, ease-in-out, or <shape>-<family> (e.g. out-expo) or cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2) or speed(out,out-reach,in,in-reach) or steps(n) or spring(bounce)
`fade 12f 10f` → duration given twice: `12f` and `10f`; expected `<preset> [<n>px] [<n>f|<n>s] [<curve>] [@<time>] [char|char-no-space|word|line] [stagger <time>] [first|last|center|edges|random]`, e.g. `fade-up 40px 12f ease-out @0f` or `fade-up word stagger 3f`; a curve is a name such as `ease-out`, `out-expo` or `hold`, `out-back(2)`, `steps(4)`, `spring(.3)`, or `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)`
`fade ease-in cubic(.2,0,0,1)` → curve given twice: `ease-in` and `cubic(.2,0,0,1)`; expected `<preset> [<n>px] [<n>f|<n>s] [<curve>] [@<time>] [char|char-no-space|word|line] [stagger <time>] [first|last|center|edges|random]`, e.g. `fade-up 40px 12f ease-out @0f` or `fade-up word stagger 3f`; a curve is a name such as `ease-out`, `out-expo` or `hold`, `out-back(2)`, `steps(4)`, `spring(.3)`, or `cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2)`

## track
`` → missing the start value in ``; expected "<value> -> <value>[@<n>%] ... -> <value> @<start>-<end> [<curve>]", e.g. "0 -> 1 @0-12f ease-out", "0 -> 200@40% -> 150 @0-30f" or "rest+40 -> rest @0-12f"
`0 1 @0-5f` → missing `->` after the start value in `0 1 @0-5f`; expected "<value> -> <value>[@<n>%] ... -> <value> @<start>-<end> [<curve>]", e.g. "0 -> 1 @0-12f ease-out", "0 -> 200@40% -> 150 @0-30f" or "rest+40 -> rest @0-12f"
`0 -> 1` → missing `@<start>-<end>` after the end value in `0 -> 1`; expected "<value> -> <value>[@<n>%] ... -> <value> @<start>-<end> [<curve>]", e.g. "0 -> 1 @0-12f ease-out", "0 -> 200@40% -> 150 @0-30f" or "rest+40 -> rest @0-12f"
`0 -> 1 2 @0-5f` → missing `@<start>-<end>` after the end value in `0 -> 1 2 @0-5f`; expected "<value> -> <value>[@<n>%] ... -> <value> @<start>-<end> [<curve>]", e.g. "0 -> 1 @0-12f ease-out", "0 -> 200@40% -> 150 @0-30f" or "rest+40 -> rest @0-12f"
`0 -> 1 @0-5f bouncy` → unknown curve `bouncy`; expected one of linear, hold, ease, ease-in, ease-out, ease-in-out, or <shape>-<family> (e.g. out-expo) or cubic(x1,y1,x2,y2) or speed(out,out-reach,in,in-reach) or steps(n) or spring(bounce)
`0 -> 1 @0-5f ease ease` → unexpected `ease` after the curve; expected "<value> -> <value>[@<n>%] ... -> <value> @<start>-<end> [<curve>]", e.g. "0 -> 1 @0-12f ease-out", "0 -> 200@40% -> 150 @0-30f" or "rest+40 -> rest @0-12f"
`0 -> 1@50% -> 2@40% -> 3 @0-10f` → `2@40%`: positions run forward, strictly between 0% and 100%, each after the one before it; expected "<value> -> <value>[@<n>%] ... -> <value> @<start>-<end> [<curve>]", e.g. "0 -> 1 @0-12f ease-out", "0 -> 200@40% -> 150 @0-30f" or "rest+40 -> rest @0-12f"
`0@10% -> 1 @0-10f` → `0@10%`: the first value falls at the start and the last at the end, so only a value between them takes a position; expected "<value> -> <value>[@<n>%] ... -> <value> @<start>-<end> [<curve>]", e.g. "0 -> 1 @0-12f ease-out", "0 -> 200@40% -> 150 @0-30f" or "rest+40 -> rest @0-12f"
`0 -> 1@half -> 2 @0-10f` → `1@half` is not a position; a value says where it falls as `@<n>%`; expected "<value> -> <value>[@<n>%] ... -> <value> @<start>-<end> [<curve>]", e.g. "0 -> 1 @0-12f ease-out", "0 -> 200@40% -> 150 @0-30f" or "rest+40 -> rest @0-12f"
`0 -> 1 -> @0-10f` → missing a value after the last `->` in `0 -> 1 -> @0-10f`; expected "<value> -> <value>[@<n>%] ... -> <value> @<start>-<end> [<curve>]", e.g. "0 -> 1 @0-12f ease-out", "0 -> 200@40% -> 150 @0-30f" or "rest+40 -> rest @0-12f"

## labels
`[]` → labels: invalid type: sequence; expected an object of named moments, e.g. {"intro":"0.5s","cta":"6s","outro":"cta+2s"}
`{"part-2":"1s"}` → labels.part-2: `part-2` is not a valid label name; expected label names use lowercase letters, digits and `_`, starting with a letter
`{"a":"b","b":"a+1f"}` → labels.a: labels in a circle: a → b → a; expected labels that each lead back to a time
`{"a":"<"}` → labels.a: a label cannot follow a layer, as `<` does; expected a time, or another label moved by a time
`{"a":"soon"}` → labels.a: unknown label `soon`; expected one of a

## relative times
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","offset":"<"}` → a.offset: `<` follows the layer before, and this layer is the first; expected a time or a label on the first layer
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","span":"intro-2s"}` → a.span: unknown label `intro`: the composition has no labels; expected a label in the composition's "labels", e.g. "labels":{"intro":"0.5s"}
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","offset":"Intro"}` → a.offset: `Intro` is not a time or a moment; expected a time such as `2s` or `-6f`, or a base moved by a time: a label (`cta`, `cta+12f`, `cta-0.5s`), `<` where the layer before ends (`<+6f`) or `<<` where it starts (`<<-3f`)
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","span":"intro"}` → a.span: `intro` is not a span; expected `<start>-<end>`, each a time or a base moved by a time, e.g. `0-30f`, `intro-cta`, `<-<+2s` or `cta-6f-outro`; a bare start takes the end's unit

## contents
`{"id":"a","shapes":[],"comp":"x"}` → a.comp: needs exactly one of `text`, `rect`, `shapes`, `comp`, `image`, `video`, `audio` or `pivot`, or only `fx` for a filter layer; expected e.g. "text":"Hello", "rect":"300x100", "shapes":[…], "comp":"card", "image":"photo.jpg", "video":"clip.mov", "audio":"music.mp3" or "pivot":true
`{"id":"a","pivot":false}` → a.pivot: `pivot` is `true` or left out; expected "pivot":true
`{"id":"a","pivot":true,"fill":"#fff"}` → a.fill: `fill` only applies to `text` or `rect` layers; expected `fill` only next to `text` or `rect`
`{"id":"a","shapes":{}}` → a.shapes: invalid type: map; expected a list of item objects, e.g. [{"rect":[300,100]},{"fill":"#FFE000"}]
`{"id":"a","comp":"nowhere"}` → a.comp: unknown composition `nowhere`: the scene has none; expected a composition under "comps", e.g. "comps":{"card":{"size":"600x400","dur":"5s","layers":[]}}
`{"id":"a","pivot":true,"hidden":1}` → a.hidden: invalid type: integer `1`; expected a boolean

## shapes
`1` → a.shapes[0]: invalid type: integer `1`; expected an item object keyed by its kind, e.g. {"rect":[300,100],"round":12} or {"fill":"#FFE000"}
`{}` → a.shapes[0]: needs the key of its kind; expected one kind key: `group`, `rect`, `ellipse`, `path`, `fill`, `stroke`, `trim`
`{"round":3}` → a.shapes[0]: needs the key of its kind; expected one kind key: `group`, `rect`, `ellipse`, `path`, `fill`, `stroke`, `trim`
`{"rect":[1,1],"fill":"#fff"}` → a.shapes[0].fill: `rect` and `fill` are both kinds; an item has one; expected one kind key: `group`, `rect`, `ellipse`, `path`, `fill`, `stroke`, `trim`
`{"rect":[1,1],"size":[2,2]}` → a.shapes[0].size: `size` is the value `rect` holds; expected `size` written as the value of `rect`
`{"rect":[1,1],"colour":1}` → a.shapes[0].colour: unknown rect key `colour`; expected one of rect, id, hidden, anim, position, round
`{"rect":[-1,1]}` → a.shapes[0].rect: value -1 is outside 0..; expected a number of at least 0
`{"rect":"wide"}` → a.shapes[0].rect: `wide` is not a point; expected a point, `[x, y]` in JSON or `x,y` in a string, e.g. `[540, 960]`
`{"rect":[1,1],"round":-2}` → a.shapes[0].round: value -2 is outside 0..; expected a number of at least 0
`{"group":{}}` → a.shapes[0].group: invalid type: map; expected a list of item objects, e.g. [{"rect":[300,100]},{"fill":"#FFE000"}]
`{"group":[{"rect":[1,1],"cap":"round"}]}` → a.shapes[0].group[0].cap: unknown rect key `cap`; expected one of rect, id, hidden, anim, position, round
`{"stroke":"#000","cap":"pointy"}` → a.shapes[0].cap: unknown stroke cap `pointy`; expected one of butt, round, square
`{"stroke":"#000","cap":1}` → a.shapes[0].cap: invalid type: integer `1`; expected a string
`{"stroke":"#000","miter":0.5}` → a.shapes[0].miter: value 0.5 is outside 1..; expected a number of at least 1
`{"fill":"#fff","id":"Bad"}` → a.shapes[0].id: invalid id `Bad`; expected ids use lowercase letters, digits, `-` and `_`, starting with a letter
`{"fill":"#fff","id":"f"},{"group":[{"fill":"#000","id":"f"}]}` → a.shapes[1].group[0].id: duplicate item id `f`; expected every item of a layer to have its own id
`{"path":[1,2]}` → a.shapes[0].path: a path is written as a string of path data, not numbers; expected SVG path data with absolute commands, e.g. `M0,0 C10,0 20,10 20,20 L0,20 Z`: `M` once, then `L x,y` or `C x1,y1 x2,y2 x,y`, and `Z` to close
`{"path":"M0,0 Q1,1 2,2"}` → a.shapes[0].path: `M0,0 Q1,1 2,2` has a command other than `L`, `C` or `Z`; expected SVG path data with absolute commands, e.g. `M0,0 C10,0 20,10 20,20 L0,20 Z`: `M` once, then `L x,y` or `C x1,y1 x2,y2 x,y`, and `Z` to close
`{"path":"M0,0 L1,1","anim":{"path":"M0,0 L1,1 -> M0,0 L2,2 @0-5f"}}` → a.shapes[0].anim.path: `path` is a path, which a key list animates; expected a list of keys like [[0, 0], ["12f", 1, "ease-out"]]
`{"path":"M0,0 L1,1","anim":{"path":[{"t":0,"v":"M0,0 L1,1"},{"t":5,"v":"M0,0 L1,1 Z"}]}}` → a.shapes[0].anim.path[1]: a path key differs in vertex count or closure from the first key; expected keys whose paths have the same vertices, all open or all closed
`{"path":"M0,0 L1,1","anim":{"path":[{"t":0,"v":"M0,0 L1,1","curve":["ease","ease"]}]}}` → a.shapes[0].anim.path[0].curve: `path` is a path, so one curve eases every vertex together; expected one curve
`{"rect":[1,1],"anim":{"opacity":"0 -> 1 @0-5f"}}` → a.shapes[0].anim.opacity: unknown rect property `opacity`; expected one of size, position, round, width, height, x, y
`{"rect":[1,1],"anim":{"width":"0 -> 1 @0-5f","size":"0,0 -> 1,1 @0-5f"}}` → a.shapes[0].anim.size: `width` and `size` both animate `size`; expected `size` animated whole, or its components `width`, `height` one at a time
`{"fill":"#fff","anim":{"color":"#000 -> 2,0,0 @0-5f"}}` → a.shapes[0].anim.color: value 2 is outside 0..=1; expected a number from 0 to 1

## text
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","style":{"tracking":1}}` → a.style: `style` only applies to `text` layers; expected `style` only next to `text`
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","box":[1,1]}` → a.box: `box` only applies to `text` or `image` or `video` layers; expected `box` only next to `text` or `image` or `video`
`{"id":"a","text":"x","style":[]}` → a.style: invalid type: sequence; expected an object of text style keys, e.g. {"tracking":20,"align":"center"}
`{"id":"a","text":"x","style":{"font":"Inter 9"}}` → a.style.font: `font` is set on the layer, not in `style`; expected `font` as a layer key
`{"id":"a","text":"x","style":{"kerning":1}}` → a.style.kerning: unknown style key `kerning`; expected one of font, italic, fill, stroke, stroke-width, paint, tracking, leading, baseline, caps, faux-bold, faux-italic, align, indent-first, indent-start, indent-end, space-before, space-after, auto-leading
`{"id":"a","text":"x","style":{"tracking":"wide"}}` → a.style.tracking: invalid type: string "wide"; expected a number
`{"id":"a","text":"x","style":{"caps":"loud"}}` → a.style.caps: unknown caps `loud`; expected one of normal, small, all, all-small
`{"id":"a","text":"x","style":{"leading":"tall"}}` → a.style.leading: invalid type: string "tall"; expected `auto` or a number of px
`{"id":"a","text":"x","style":{"stroke":[2,0,0]}}` → a.style.stroke: a colour channel is outside 0 to 1; expected a colour: `#RGB`, `#RRGGBB`, `#RRGGBBAA`, or `[r, g, b, a]` with each channel 0 to 1
`{"id":"a","text":"x","style":{"stroke-width":-1}}` → a.style.stroke-width: -1 is below 0; expected a number of at least 0
`{"id":"a","text":"x","style":{"faux-bold":"yes"}}` → a.style.faux-bold: invalid type: string "yes"; expected a boolean
`{"id":"a","text":"x","fill":[1,0]}` → a.fill: 2 numbers do not make a colour; expected a colour: `#RGB`, `#RRGGBB`, `#RRGGBBAA`, or `[r, g, b, a]` with each channel 0 to 1
`{"id":"a","text":"x","runs":{}}` → a.runs: invalid type: map; expected a list of style objects, e.g. [{"range":[0,4],"fill":"#FF0000"}]
`{"id":"a","text":"x","runs":[{"fill":"#FFF"}]}` → a.runs[0]: missing `range`; expected `[start, end]`, character indices with start before end, e.g. `[0, 4]`
`{"id":"a","text":"x","runs":[{"range":[1,1]}]}` → a.runs[0].range: the range must run forward over whole indices; expected `[start, end]`, character indices with start before end, e.g. `[0, 4]`
`{"id":"a","text":"x","runs":[{"range":[0,2]}]}` → a.runs[0].range: the range ends at 2, past the text's 1 characters; expected `[start, end]`, character indices with start before end, e.g. `[0, 4]`
`{"id":"a","text":"x","runs":[{"range":[0,0.5]}]}` → a.runs[0].range: the range must run forward over whole indices; expected `[start, end]`, character indices with start before end, e.g. `[0, 4]`
`{"id":"a","text":"x","runs":[{"range":"0-1"}]}` → a.runs[0].range: invalid type: string "0-1"; expected `[start, end]`, character indices with start before end, e.g. `[0, 4]`
`{"id":"a","text":"x","runs":[{"range":[0,1],"align":"center"}]}` → a.runs[0].align: `align` cannot be set on a run; expected `align` in `style` or `paragraphs`
`{"id":"a","text":"x","paragraphs":[{"tracking":3}]}` → a.paragraphs[0].tracking: `tracking` cannot be set on a paragraph; expected `tracking` in `style` or `runs`
`{"id":"a","text":"x","paragraphs":[{},{}]}` → a.paragraphs: 2 paragraph styles for 1 paragraphs; expected at most one style per paragraph; `\n` ends a paragraph
`{"id":"a","text":"x","paragraphs":[{"align":"middle"}]}` → a.paragraphs[0].align: unknown alignment `middle`; expected one of left, right, center, justify-left, justify-right, justify-center, justify-all
`{"id":"a","text":"x","box":[0,10]}` → a.box: a box's width and height are above zero; expected `[width, height]` from the layer's origin, or `[x, y, width, height]` from the box's top-left corner, in px, the sizes above zero, e.g. `[600, 300]` or `[-300, -150, 600, 300]`
`{"id":"a","text":"x","box":"wide"}` → a.box: a box is two or four numbers; expected `[width, height]` from the layer's origin, or `[x, y, width, height]` from the box's top-left corner, in px, the sizes above zero, e.g. `[600, 300]` or `[-300, -150, 600, 300]`

## animators
`{"id":"a","rect":"1x1","animate":[]}` → a.animate: `animate` only applies to `text` layers; expected `animate` only next to `text`
`{"id":"a","text":"x","animate":[{"range":"char"}]}` → a.animate[0]: needs the key of its kind; expected one kind key: `animator`
`{"id":"a","text":"x","animate":[{"animator":{}}]}` → a.animate[0].animator: invalid type: map; expected a list of item objects, e.g. [{"rect":[300,100]},{"fill":"#FFE000"}]
`{"id":"a","text":"x","animate":[{"animator":[{"rect":[1,1]}]}]}` → a.animate[0].animator[0]: needs the key of its kind; expected one kind key: `range`
`{"id":"a","text":"x","animate":[{"animator":[{"range":"sentence"}]}]}` → a.animate[0].animator[0].range: unknown range by `sentence`; expected one of char, char-no-space, word, line
`{"id":"a","text":"x","animate":[{"animator":[{"range":"char","by":"word"}]}]}` → a.animate[0].animator[0].by: `by` is the value `range` holds; expected `by` written as the value of `range`
`{"id":"a","text":"x","animate":[{"animator":[{"range":"char","offset":2}]}]}` → a.animate[0].animator[0].offset: value 2 is outside -1..=1; expected a number from -1 to 1
`{"id":"a","text":"x","animate":[{"animator":[{"range":"char","shape":"wave"}]}]}` → a.animate[0].animator[0].shape: unknown range shape `wave`; expected one of square, ramp-up, ramp-down, triangle, round, smooth
`{"id":"a","text":"x","animate":[{"animator":[],"y":3}]}` → a.animate[0].y: unknown animator key `y`; expected one of animator, id, hidden, anim, by, order, position, anchor, scale, rotate, opacity, fill, stroke, stroke-width, tracking, stagger, seed
`{"id":"a","text":"x","animate":[{"animator":[],"opacity":2}]}` → a.animate[0].opacity: value 2 is outside 0..=1; expected a number from 0 to 1
`{"id":"a","text":"x","animate":[{"animator":[],"anim":{"glow":"0 -> 1 @0-5f"}}]}` → a.animate[0].anim.glow: unknown animator property `glow`; expected one of position, anchor, scale, rotate, opacity, fill, stroke, stroke-width, tracking, stagger, seed, x, y, anchor-x, anchor-y, scale-x, scale-y

## fonts
`{"motion":1,"dur":"1s","fonts":"fonts","layers":[]}` → fonts: invalid type: string "fonts"; expected a list of font files and folders, e.g. ["fonts/lato"]
`{"motion":1,"dur":"1s","fonts":[3],"layers":[]}` → fonts[0]: invalid type: integer `3`; expected a string

## effects
`{"rect":[1,1]}` → a.fx[0]: needs the key of its kind; expected one kind key: `fill`, `transform`, `tint`, `hue-saturation`, `exposure`, `levels`, `particles`, `displacement-map`, `audio-spectrum`, `audio-waveform`, `motion-tile`, `wrap`, `turbulent-displace`, `ramp`, `four-color`, `grid`, `venetian-blinds`, `fractal-noise`, `gaussian-blur`, `box-blur`, `drop-shadow`, `glow`, `sharpen`, `black-white`, `curves`, `invert`
`{"fill":"#fff","opacity":3}` → a.fx[0].opacity: value 3 is outside 0..=1; expected a number from 0 to 1
`{"fill":"#fff","rule":"evenodd"}` → a.fx[0].rule: unknown fill key `rule`; expected one of fill, id, hidden, anim, opacity

## comps
`"card":1` → comps.card: invalid type: integer `1`; expected a composition object, e.g. {"size":"600x400","dur":"5s","layers":[]}
`"Card":{"size":"1x1","dur":"1s","layers":[]}` → comps.Card: invalid composition id `Card`; expected ids use lowercase letters, digits, `-` and `_`, starting with a letter
`"card":{"dur":"1s","layers":[]}` → comps.card: missing `size`; expected e.g. "size":"1080x1920"
`"card":{"size":"1x1","layers":[]}` → comps.card: missing `dur`; expected e.g. "dur":"5s"
`"card":{"size":"1x1","dur":"1s"}` → comps.card: missing `layers`; expected e.g. "layers":[]
`"card":{"size":"1x1","dur":"1s","fps":0,"layers":[]}` → comps.card.fps: must be a number above zero; expected e.g. `30`
`"card":{"size":"1x1","dur":"1s","layers":[],"tint":1}` → comps.card.tint: unknown field `tint`; expected one of size, fps, dur, bg, shutter, labels, slots, layers
`"card":{"size":"1x1","dur":"1s","layers":[{"id":"x"}]}` → comps.card.layers[x]: needs exactly one of `text`, `rect`, `shapes`, `comp`, `image`, `video`, `audio` or `pivot`, or only `fx` for a filter layer; expected e.g. "text":"Hello", "rect":"300x100", "shapes":[…], "comp":"card", "image":"photo.jpg", "video":"clip.mov", "audio":"music.mp3" or "pivot":true
`"card":{"size":"1x1","dur":"1s","layers":[{"id":"x","comp":"card"}]}` → comps.card.layers[x].comp: composition `card` would draw itself through its layers; expected compositions that never lead back to themselves
`"card":{"size":"1x1","dur":"1s","layers":[{"id":"x","comp":"b"}]},"b":{"size":"1x1","dur":"1s","layers":[{"id":"y","comp":"card"}]}` → comps.card.layers[x].comp: composition `card` would draw itself through its layers; expected compositions that never lead back to themselves

## range
`@x-5f` → `@x-5f` is not a valid range; expected `@<start>-<end>` with a unit, e.g. `@0-30f`, `@0.5s-1s`
`@05f` → `@05f` has no `-` between start and end; expected `@<start>-<end>` with a unit, e.g. `@0-30f`, `@0.5s-1s`
`@0-5` → `@0-5` needs a unit (`f` or `s`) after the end; expected `@<start>-<end>` with a unit, e.g. `@0-30f`, `@0.5s-1s`

## span
`x-5f` → `x-5f` is not a valid range; expected `<start>-<end>` with a unit, e.g. `0-30f`, `0.5s-1s`; a bare start takes the end's unit
`05f` → `05f` has no `-` between start and end; expected `<start>-<end>` with a unit, e.g. `0-30f`, `0.5s-1s`; a bare start takes the end's unit
`0-5` → `0-5` needs a unit (`f` or `s`) after the end; expected `<start>-<end>` with a unit, e.g. `0-30f`, `0.5s-1s`; a bare start takes the end's unit
`@0-5f` → `@0-5f` is not a valid range; expected `<start>-<end>` with a unit, e.g. `0-30f`, `0.5s-1s`; a bare start takes the end's unit

## address
`` → `` is not a valid address; expected `scene` or layer ids joined by `/`, then `.key`s, each with an optional `[id]` or `[index]`, e.g. `card/title.fx[glow].radius`
`scene/card` → `scene/card` is not a valid address; expected `scene` or layer ids joined by `/`, then `.key`s, each with an optional `[id]` or `[index]`, e.g. `card/title.fx[glow].radius`
`card.fx[glow` → `card.fx[glow` is not a valid address; expected `scene` or layer ids joined by `/`, then `.key`s, each with an optional `[id]` or `[index]`, e.g. `card/title.fx[glow].radius`

## id
`Card` → invalid id `Card`; expected ids use lowercase letters, digits, `-` and `_`, starting with a letter

## serde
`{}` → missing field `key`
`"dim"` → unknown variant `dim`; expected one of on
